      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Myocardial contractile capacity was studied in 100 patients with ischemic heart disease who had suffered from myocardial infarction. All of them were subjected to electrocardiography, selective coronarography and left ventriculography. Depending on the entirety of the affection of the coronary channel the patients were grouped in four caterogies. The authors claim that determination of the entirety of the affection of coronary arteries in patients with ischemic heart disease who had suffered from myocardial infarction helps to judge the contractile capacity of the myocardium with a greater degree of credibility."},
